From: soralis0912 <soralis.nem@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bundle an AudioParaManger stub for the cinematic recorder

The cinematic (movie) mode recorder builds an inner class that
implements android.media.AudioParaManger$TuneListener in its constructor.
That class comes from MIUI's miui-framework.jar, which is on the stock
BOOTCLASSPATH and is absent here, so the constructor throws
NoClassDefFoundError. RxJava swallows it, the module switch never
completes, and the viewfinder stays blurred forever.

Ship the class inside the APK the same way it already ships
android.media.MediaCinematic. The boot class loader does not have it, so
the app's own copy is used. It behaves like stock on a device without
the vendor audio-zoom effect: init() fails and recording falls back to
plain audio. The other video modes only probe for the class reflectively
and are unaffected.

Place the compatibility classes in a new classes8 dex to avoid the
method-reference limits of the stock dex files. Ported from degas and
warhol; the methods cover the klimt APK references.

diff --git a/smali_classes8/android/media/AudioParaManger$EventListener.smali b/smali_classes8/android/media/AudioParaManger$EventListener.smali
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7f0aa1e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/smali_classes8/android/media/AudioParaManger$EventListener.smali
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+.class public interface abstract Landroid/media/AudioParaManger$EventListener;
+.super Ljava/lang/Object;
+.source "AudioParaManger.java"
+
+
+# annotations
+.annotation system Ldalvik/annotation/EnclosingClass;
+    value = Landroid/media/AudioParaManger;
+.end annotation
+
+.annotation system Ldalvik/annotation/InnerClass;
+    accessFlags = 0x609
+    name = "EventListener"
+.end annotation
+
+
+# virtual methods
+.method public onAudioLevel(II)V
+    .registers 3
+
+    return-void
+.end method
+
+.method public abstract onMicBlocking(II)V
+.end method
